**Peak geometry (EUV-legal):** the quantity that tracks *peak* speed, not mean speed, is coronal-hole **longitudinal width Δθ** (Garton: \(v_\mathrm{max}=330.8+5.7\Delta\theta\) until ~710 km/s; Samara: peak vs long-ext cc=0.57 vs area 0.50 vs lat 0.41). Next is Hofmeister **area × co-latitude** (RMSE 70, cc=0.70). Central-meridian slice area (Vršnak/Rotter/ESWF) is a 4-day *profile* predictor; OLS on it “smooths out peak values.” Scatter floor is ~70–118 km/s even with isolated-CH pairing.

**Illegal, skipped:** magnetograms/WSA, 27-day V, 171Å (CHIMERA), sunspot number, OMNI N/T/B, B0.

**Why MSE never reaches peaks:** it is \(E[Y|X]\), i.e. the slow-wind mean. Collin’s Box-Cox *post-hoc* lifts peak RMSE ~23% and **worsens** timeline RMSE — closed for us. Open, in-training options with no extra data: expectile/pinball \(q>0.5\), two-Gaussian MDN (take \(\mu_\mathrm{fast}\), not the mixture mean), two-head peak+shape. No published solar-wind RMSE for expectile/MDN.

**Ensembles:** the bag mean is the same conditional mean, so it damps HSS amplitude (Riley/Owens; Hegde; Reiss WSA std 70 vs ACE 84). Counter: do not mean-blend the optical-flow/Stonyhurst members with tabular GBDT on fast cells; gate or take a high-q/MDN-fast output on CH-wide rows.
